WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.550
In five minutes, I found a

2
00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:04.510
stranger's school, her birthday

3
00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:06.750
and the street she walks home on.

4
00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:08.270
I never met her.

5
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.880
I only read her public posts.

6
00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:15.340
Today: your digital footprint, and how

7
00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:16.640
to make it say what you want.

8
00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:20.090
Everything you do online leaves a

9
00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:22.790
trace, and together those traces

10
00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:24.210
are your digital footprint.

11
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.520
Some you leave on purpose: posts,

12
00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:30.060
comments, photos and voice notes.

13
00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:31.950
That's your active footprint.

14
00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:34.750
Others you leave without noticing:

15
00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:37.470
where your phone goes, what you search

16
00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.610
for, what you like and watch.

17
00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:41.810
That's your passive footprint.

18
00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:46.340
A footprint in sand washes away, but

19
00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:48.480
an online one usually stays.

20
00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:50.730
A friend can screenshot your

21
00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:51.870
post in one second.

22
00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:54.690
By evening, a group chat can

23
00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:56.490
forward it to hundreds of people.

24
00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:59.720
Deleting your copy doesn't delete theirs.

25
00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:02.470
Here's what most people miss.

26
00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:06.660
One detail on its own looks harmless: your

27
00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:09.380
school uniform in one photo, your birthday

28
00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:12.020
in another, your bus stop in a third.

29
00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:15.240
Put together, they tell a stranger who you

30
00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:17.740
are, where to find you, and when.

31
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.580
It's like a jigsaw puzzle.

32
00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:24.200
One piece shows nothing, but every

33
00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:26.880
post adds a piece, and a patient

34
00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:28.780
stranger can finish the picture.

35
00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:31.690
Even your pet's name is a piece, because

36
00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:33.370
it's a common answer to the security

37
00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:34.890
questions that reset passwords.

38
00:01:36.290 --> 00:01:36.690
Quick check!

39
00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:39.190
Which of these is safest to

40
00:01:39.190 --> 00:01:40.270
put on a public profile?

41
00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:42.710
Your favourite book.

42
00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:45.760
It says what you like, not where

43
00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:47.420
you are or when you're alone.

44
00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:50.450
Before you post, try the

45
00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:51.530
three-people test.

46
00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:53.840
Would you be happy if your

47
00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:54.840
grandmother saw it?

48
00:01:55.390 --> 00:01:56.170
Your head teacher?

49
00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:58.900
A stranger who wants to find you?

50
00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:02.520
If any answer is no, change it, or

51
00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:03.800
keep it for close friends.

52
00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:07.170
Your footprint can work for you, too.

53
00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:09.470
Think of a science project you're

54
00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:12.150
proud of, a kind comment, or a

55
00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:12.910
skill you're learning.

56
00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:15.670
One day a school or an employer

57
00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:17.870
may search your name, so give them

58
00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:19.010
something good to find.

59
00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:20.730
Your turn.

60
00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:22.780
You delete an embarrassing

61
00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:24.420
post after one hour.

62
00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:26.240
Is it gone for good?

63
00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:30.080
Not for sure, because in one hour

64
00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:32.340
someone may have saved or shared it.

65
00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:36.220
Remember: everything leaves a trace, small

66
00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:40.220
details add up, test before you post, and

67
00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:42.140
make your footprint work for you.

68
00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:45.430
Try it tomorrow: look at your

69
00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:47.590
profile the way a stranger would.

70
00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:49.730
Count the posts that show your

71
00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:52.470
school, your street or your routine,

72
00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:54.790
and hide or delete one of them.
